00:07:50.899 --> 00:08:01.740
Yeah, so if you listen to the show, uh, one of the first, uh, the things you'll hear, uh, is we often will play a voice note or a voice memo from, uh, a fan from all over the world.
好的，如果你收听这个节目，嗯，你会听到的第一批事情之一，就是我们经常会播放来自世界各地粉丝的语音留言或语音备忘录。

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:03.980
we've heard from people all over the world.
我们听到了来自世界各地人们的声音。

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:07.579
And the prompt is essentially, what is how I met your mother mean to you?
而提示基本上是，《老爸老妈浪漫史》对你意味着什么？

00:08:07.579 --> 00:08:09.500
Just tell us what the show means to you.
只需告诉我们这部剧对你意味着什么。

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:15.899
And we've gotten the most extraordinary, beautiful, heartfelt, amazing letters.
我们收到了非常非凡、美丽、真挚、惊艳的信件。

00:08:15.899 --> 00:08:16.819
So that's a voice memo.
所以那是语音备忘录。

00:08:16.819 --> 00:08:30.620
If you want us to potentially play your voice memo on air, I'll tell you how in one second, but you can also write us a letter, good old fashioned email.
如果你希望我们在节目中播放你的语音备忘录，我一会儿告诉你怎么做，但你也可以给我们写信，通过老式的电子邮件。

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:40.100
So go to how we made your mother.com or HWMYM.com, go to contact and just follow the instructions.
所以访问 how we made your mother.com 或 HWMYM.com，点击联系我们，然后按照说明操作。

00:08:40.100 --> 00:08:42.299
It should be pretty self-explanatory.
这应该是不言自明的。

00:08:42.299 --> 00:08:43.299
But we'd love to hear from you.
但我们很想听到你的声音。

00:08:43.299 --> 00:08:45.620
So, yeah, send us that.
所以，是的，给我们发信息吧。

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:47.500
It's by far the best, our favorite part.
这绝对是最好、最让我们喜爱的一部分。

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:48.500
It's the best part of doing this.
这是做这件事最棒的部分。

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:52.299
It's hearing from the fans, and it's always a big part of every episode of the podcast.
那就是倾听粉丝的心声，这也一直是播客每期节目的重要组成部分。

00:08:52.299 --> 00:08:56.240
So get involved, come listen, and yeah, join us there.
所以参与进来，来收听吧，是的，加入我们。

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:57.080
What else have we got, Alec?
我们还有什么，亚历克？

00:08:57.080 --> 00:08:58.679
How do we answer questions now?
我们现在怎么回答问题？

00:08:58.679 --> 00:09:00.759
Well, we could do that.
嗯，我们可以这么做。

00:09:00.759 --> 00:09:09.720
First of all, by the way, let's just have a conversation with our friend here, Alex Lourdes, who was wondering if this was live, who says the intro was so smooth, I thought it was pre-recorded.
首先，顺便说一句，让我们先和我们的朋友亚历克斯·劳尔德斯（Alex Lourdes）聊聊，他刚刚还在纳闷这到底是不是直播，他说开场太流畅了，他还以为是录播呢。

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:12.279
So, right, probably right up until the...
所以，对吧，大概直到……

00:09:12.279 --> 00:09:15.559
It was really, it fooled me until you guys shot the bed with the battery tray.
真的很厉害，在你们因为电池问题搞砸之前，我都被骗了。

00:09:15.559 --> 00:09:23.600
When it would be amazing if it was pre-recorded, but we were such geniuses that we built in the iPhone debacle.
如果这是录播就太棒了，而我们又是如此天才，竟然把 iPhone 的闹剧给设计进去了。

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:24.440
Yeah.
对。

00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:26.179
On the block.
在区里。

00:09:26.179 --> 00:09:44.220
Okay, so here's just a lovely question here from I Am Nina Now says from Buenos Aires, although not exactly the question, I want to thank Josh for writing kind over matter on a piece of paper a few years ago so I could get it tattooed.
好的，这里有一个来自“我是现在的妮娜”的可爱问题，她说来自布宜诺斯艾利斯，虽然不完全是这个问题，但我要感谢乔斯几年前在一张纸上写下“随缘善念”（kind over matter），好让我能把它纹在身上。

00:09:44.220 --> 00:09:51.500
Wow, was that in, I wonder if it was in Buenos Aires when Ben Lee and I played there in like maybe 2017?
哇，那是，我不知道是不是在布宜诺斯艾利斯，当时本·李和我大概在 2017 年在那里演出？

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:53.460
Let us know, yeah, yeah, yeah.
让我们知道，对，对，对。

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:55.620
That's awesome, we'd love to see the tattoo.
太棒了，我们很想看看这个纹身。

00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:58.379
Yeah, a lot of tattoos, right Craig?
对，有很多纹身，对吧，克雷格？

00:09:58.379 --> 00:10:02.059
We've seen so many of how I met your mother-related tattoos.
我们见过太多与《老爸老妈浪漫史》相关的纹身了。

00:10:02.059 --> 00:10:02.899
It's crazy.
太疯狂了。

00:10:02.899 --> 00:10:06.299
That wasn't exactly that instance.
那倒不完全是那个情况。

00:10:06.299 --> 00:10:07.779
That was something Josh did that was awesome.
那是乔斯做过的一件很棒的事。

00:10:07.779 --> 00:10:10.580
But him and fans are sending us some pretty.
但他和粉丝们给我们发了一些相当……

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:12.379
A lot of yellow umbrella.
有很多黄色雨伞。

00:10:12.379 --> 00:10:16.899
Lou French horn speaking of quotes from the show.
说到剧中的台词，还有法国号。

00:10:16.899 --> 00:10:17.740
All kinds of stuff.
各种各样的东西。

00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:20.659
What an honor for things from the show to be on somebody's body.
剧中物品能出现在别人的身体上，是多么荣幸的一件事。

00:10:20.659 --> 00:10:21.899
That's a fan.
那才是粉丝。

00:10:21.899 --> 00:10:24.700
That's a real fan.
那才是真正的粉丝。

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:34.730
And I wrote you this little ditty to send you in New York City.
我为你写了这首小曲，送给远在纽约的你。

00:10:34.730 --> 00:10:38.350
We'll be right back.
我们马上回来。

00:10:38.350 --> 00:10:42.190
Hi, I'm Alex Goldman, host of the Hyper-Fixed podcast.
嗨，我是亚历克斯·戈德曼，是“超级修复”（Hyper-Fixed）播客的主持人。

00:10:42.190 --> 00:10:45.669
Each week, we take listeners' problems and try to solve them for them.
每周，我们都会接受听众的求助并努力为他们解决问题。

00:10:45.669 --> 00:10:48.830
Problems like, I'm 30, and I'm scared to drive in New York.
比如这样的问题：我 30 岁了，但害怕在纽约开车。

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:52.629
Or, why can't I adjust the volume of my car stereo when I'm in reverse?
或者，为什么倒车时我无法调节车载音响的音量？

00:10:52.629 --> 00:10:55.149
We also solve non-car related problems.
我们也解决与汽车无关的问题。

00:10:55.149 --> 00:11:01.259
If you have a problem, not only will we fix it, we'll expose the hidden systems that cause that problem in the first place.
如果你遇到了问题，我们不仅会帮你解决，还会揭示导致该问题的隐藏系统。

00:11:01.259 --> 00:11:03.740
That's the Hyper-Fixed Podcast from Radiotopia.
这就是来自 Radiotopia 的“超级修复”播客。

00:11:03.740 --> 00:11:18.940
Find it wherever you find podcasts, or at hyperfixedpod.com.
你可以在各大播客平台或访问 hyperfixedpod.com 找到它。

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:22.299
And now, back to the show.
现在，让我们回到节目中。

00:11:22.299 --> 00:11:26.980
Okay, I'm gonna just start off with just a really big question here, because it's a lovely one.
好的，我打算以一个非常重磅的问题开始，因为这是一个很可爱的问题。

00:11:26.980 --> 00:11:32.019
It might take some time for you guys to think about, or you might have several answers to, so let's just go for it.
你们可能需要花点时间思考，或者你们有多个答案，所以我们这就开始吧。

00:11:32.019 --> 00:11:35.220
This actually comes to us from Instagram.
这个问题实际上来自我们的 Instagram。

00:11:35.220 --> 00:11:42.909
Benny Belive says, it would be so interesting to know what was your favorite day on set and why.
Benny Belive 说，真想知道你们在片场的哪一天最难忘，为什么。

00:11:42.909 --> 00:11:46.223
Is there a special day where everyone just had the best work day?
有没有那么一天，每个人都度过了最棒的工作日？

00:11:46.223 --> 00:11:49.843
Or would you say that every day of shooting was special in its own way?
或者你会说，每天的拍摄都有它独特而特殊的地方？

00:11:49.843 --> 00:11:52.750
Thank you so much for entertainment over all these years.
非常感谢你们这么多年来带给我们的欢乐。

00:11:52.750 --> 00:11:54.391
The series makes me smile.
这部剧总是能让我会心一笑。

00:11:54.391 --> 00:11:58.053
I can't, it's so cool that you're doing this here in 2026.
我真是没想到，你们竟然能在2026年在这里做这件事，太酷了。

00:11:58.053 --> 00:12:08.470
So, if you're just thinking back, especially to these first two seasons, are there days that to just pop into your mind as being memorable for one reason or another.
所以，如果你回想过去，尤其是前两季的时候，有没有哪几天，因为这样或那样的原因，突然蹦进你的脑海，让你觉得印象深刻？

00:12:10.389 --> 00:12:11.549
Yeah, that's a great question.
对，这是一个很好的问题。

00:12:11.549 --> 00:12:18.470
I think that I want to answer the second part of what he asked though about was every day the best.
不过我觉得我想回答他问的第二部分，关于是不是每天都是最好的一天。

00:12:18.470 --> 00:12:20.470
And I will say no to that.
我要说不是。

00:12:20.470 --> 00:12:24.470
And that's just, that's just because we did nine years.
这只是因为我们拍了九年。

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:34.669
And if you take a decade of your life, no matter where you are, how your work it would, like you're gonna have good days and you're gonna have not so good days, but you gotta show up at the office anyway, you know?
如果你把十年的生命投入其中，无论你在哪里，无论你的工作是什么，你都会有状态好的日子，也会有状态不那么好的日子，但你还是得去办公室上班，对吧？

00:12:34.669 --> 00:12:39.269
So you just have to bring yourself wherever you are.
所以无论你在哪，你都得打起精神来。

00:12:39.269 --> 00:12:53.070
I think when the cameras rolled, we all tried to drink the fake beer and eat the Chex mix and do our jobs and sell the jokes and authentically play our parts.
我觉得当镜头开机时，我们都努力喝着假啤酒，吃着混合零食，做好本职工作，把笑话包袱抖响，真情实感地扮演好我们的角色。

00:12:53.830 --> 00:13:08.070
But some days were hard on set and other days, I will say it wasn't all like the blooper reel, although every moment from the Bulletproof reel actually happened and was as funny and joyful as it looked, you know?
但有些天在片场确实很难熬，而另一些天……我得说，并不完全像花絮里那样轻松，尽管爆笑花絮里的每一个瞬间都是真实发生的，而且和看起来一样有趣、欢乐，对吧？

00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:16.490
So I think that when I think of like happy moments on set, for some reason, this always stays with me.
所以我想，当我回想起片场那些快乐的时刻时，出于某种原因，这个画面一直留在我心中。

00:13:16.490 --> 00:13:18.970
And I think I talked about this once on the podcast.
我想我曾在播客里提到过一次。

00:13:18.970 --> 00:13:27.370
We would often do like early morning or breakfast scenes, you know, Marshall, Lilly, and Ted in sweatpants having breakfast, you know?
我们经常要拍一些清晨或吃早餐的戏，你知道的，马修、莉莉和泰德穿着运动裤吃早餐，懂吗？

00:13:27.370 --> 00:13:30.600
We just, what happened?
我们刚刚……怎么了？

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:32.639
Josh, can you just say that last thing one more time?
乔希，你能把刚才那句最后的话再说一遍吗？

00:13:32.639 --> 00:13:34.600
we just lost your last two sentences there.
我们刚刚没听清你最后两句话。

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:35.440
Oh, okay.
哦，好吧。

00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:38.759
Well, when I think about happy moments on set, is that what you were talking about?
嗯，当我想到片场那些快乐的时刻时，你是说那个吗？

00:13:38.759 --> 00:13:39.600
Yeah.
对。

00:13:39.600 --> 00:13:54.519
When I think about happy moments on set, we often, I think I talked about this on the podcast at one point, but Jason and Ali and myself, as Ted Marshall and Lily, we would often do like breakfast scenes.
当我想到片场那些快乐的时刻时，我们经常——我想我之前在播客里也提到过——杰森、艾莉和我，作为泰德、马修和莉莉，我们经常拍那种早餐的戏。

00:13:54.519 --> 00:14:04.039
And for some reason, they would sometimes, Mike Shea, the way he structured them, the breakfast or early morning scenes would often be the first scenes of the day.
而且不知为什么，迈克·谢（Mike Shea）对它们的结构安排，早餐或清晨的戏往往会是一天中的第一场戏。

00:14:04.039 --> 00:14:15.639
So you drive to the Fox lot in Los Angeles, you'd get out of your car, you'd go through hair and makeup, and you'd go into your dressing room and you had to change into like a t-shirt and sweatpants.
所以你开车去洛杉矶的福克斯片场，下车，做发型和化妆，走进化妆间，然后你得换上一件T恤和运动裤。

00:14:15.639 --> 00:14:21.159
And then you get on set and Dave Baker, the props guy goes, what cereal do you want?
接着你来到片场，道具师戴夫·贝克（Dave Baker）就会问：“你想吃什么麦片？”

00:14:21.159 --> 00:14:22.720
What do you want in your coffee?
“你的咖啡里要加什么？”

00:14:23.879 --> 00:14:30.960
And then you would just sit there and have breakfast and drink coffee and make each other laugh.
然后你就在那里吃早餐、喝咖啡，逗彼此笑。

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:35.320
And it was just like, there were those moments where you're like, I can't believe I'm getting paid for that.
那种感觉就像是，有时候你会想：我简直不敢相信自己居然能因为这而拿到报酬。

00:14:35.320 --> 00:14:42.000
Like, I have someone's gonna come and discover that this is like too fun, like too much fun.
就像，会有什么人来发现这一切简直太有趣了，乐趣过头了。

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:47.960
It's too, it was just a blast, you know, to have that be your job, you know?
太棒了，把这当成你的工作，真的是一种享受，你知道吗？

00:14:47.960 --> 00:14:50.940
And yeah, yeah.
对，对。

00:14:50.940 --> 00:14:59.259
Yeah, I would just add on to that too and say that there would just be certain moments every so often, because you lose, it's what Josh is saying, it's your job.
对，我还要补充一点，就是每隔一段时间就会出现某些特定时刻，因为你渐渐习惯了，正如乔希所说，这就是你的工作。

00:14:59.259 --> 00:15:01.419
It's every day you start taking it for granted.
每天你都开始把它视为理所当然。

00:15:01.419 --> 00:15:05.840
It doesn't feel like showbiz every day or magical, magical every second.
它并不总是像什么好莱坞秀场，也不是每分每秒都那么神奇。

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:17.440
But every now and again, there'd be some moment where I'd just take a half step back and I'd look at Josh Radner reading dialogue that I wrote or that Carter wrote or that we all fashioned together on the writers from the day before.
但偶尔会有那么一个瞬间，我会稍微退后半步，看着乔希·拉德纳（Josh Radnor）念着我写的台词，或者卡特写的台词，又或者是我们前一天在编剧室里一起琢磨出来的台词。

00:15:17.440 --> 00:15:28.440
Josh and Kobe acting in a scene together and then they kind of zoom out and you go, and there's Pam Fryman directing it and there's our entire crew and there's Dave Baker with the Lucky Charms for whoever ordered Lucky Charms and whatever it was.
看着乔希和科比在一场戏里搭戏，然后脑海里画面拉远，你会感叹，帕姆·弗莱曼（Pam Fryman）正在导演这场戏，我们的整个剧组都在，还有带着幸运麦片（Lucky Charms）的戴夫·贝克，给任何点名要幸运麦片的人准备着，不管是谁。

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:37.440
And like every now and again, I'd sort of like grasp the totality of it and just go like, this is everyone's here on the same mission, right?
然后偶尔，我就会有一种对全局的领悟，心里就会想：大家来这里都是为了同一个目标，对吧？

00:15:37.440 --> 00:15:44.120
We all, we came up with this thing and we said, hey everybody, would you come into our little universe and yes and it and kind of play with us?
我们想出了这个点子，然后对大家说：“嘿，各位，你们愿意进入我们的小宇宙，顺着我们的设定，跟我们一起玩吗？”

00:15:44.120 --> 00:15:45.519
Like two kids playing together.
就像两个小孩在一起玩过家家一样。

00:15:45.519 --> 00:15:49.240
I think that's the spirit of like, we're gonna play, we're gonna get our Star Wars guys, we're gonna play.
我觉得这就是那种精神：我们要去玩，我们要拿出星球大战的玩偶，我们要开始玩了。

00:15:49.240 --> 00:15:53.240
And every now and again, it would occur to me, like you just said, Josh, like, how is this our job?
偶尔我会有这种感觉，就像你刚才说的，乔希：“这怎么能是我们的工作呢？”

00:15:53.240 --> 00:15:55.340
How are we able to come do this?
我们怎么能来做这个？

00:15:55.340 --> 00:16:01.100
How is everybody here agreeing this universe exists and making it up together?
为什么大家都会同意这个宇宙的存在，并一起把它编造出来？

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:04.820
And every now and again, that feeling would hit me and it was the greatest feeling.
偶尔这种感觉会涌上心头，那是最美妙的感觉。

00:16:04.820 --> 00:16:12.500
I felt that when I directed both movies I wrote, I was like, I dreamt this scene up in a coffee shop.
当我导演自己写的那两部电影时，我也有过这种感觉，我当时想：“我在一家咖啡馆里梦想出了这个场景。”

00:16:12.500 --> 00:16:13.340
Yeah.
对。

00:16:13.340 --> 00:16:16.899
This started in my imagination and now all these people are bringing it to life.
这一切始于我的想象，现在所有这些人都在把它变成现实。

00:16:16.899 --> 00:16:21.299
And I can't believe I'm looking through a camera and seeing kind of what I dreamt up, but better.
我简直不敢相信我正透过摄像机镜头，看着我曾经梦想中的画面，甚至比我想象的还要好。

00:16:21.299 --> 00:16:22.139
Better.
还要好。

00:16:22.139 --> 00:16:22.980
Yeah, that's it.
对，就是这样。

00:16:22.980 --> 00:16:28.139
That's it, it's the humbling feeling of how much better it is than you could have ever dreamt it to be.
就是这样，那种感觉会让你感到谦卑，因为它比你曾经梦想过的还要好得多。

00:16:28.139 --> 00:16:32.100
It feels, that's the magic, that's the magical piece.
那种感觉，这就是魔法，这就是神奇的部分。

00:16:32.100 --> 00:16:35.980
I will say also, there's something called, I think it's called the hedonic treadmill.
我还想说，有个概念，我想它叫“享乐适应”（hedonic treadmill）。

00:16:35.980 --> 00:16:38.139
Have you ever heard of that phrase?
你听说过这个词吗？

00:16:38.139 --> 00:16:54.059
It's basically like the things you dream about and it's basically how quickly we metabolize our good fortune that the thing you wanted five years ago, you have it and you're suddenly like, the couches here are terrible.
它基本上是指，那些你梦寐以求的东西……也就是我们习惯好运的速度有多快：你五年前想要的东西，现在你得到了，而你突然就会开始挑剔：“这里的沙发太糟糕了。”

00:16:54.059 --> 00:17:00.460
Like you just immediately go back to your same level of dissatisfaction and looking forward to the next thing.
就像你立刻又回到了原来的不满水平，然后开始期待下一件东西。

00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:09.339
And you know, I knew that this was a great gig and I knew that the writing was really sharp and I knew the cast was jelling and I knew we were firing all cylinders.
你知道的，我知道这是一个很棒的工作，我知道剧本非常犀利，我知道演员们相处融洽，我也知道我们火力全开。

00:17:09.339 --> 00:17:15.740
And still, you have days where you're like, like you're dragging your feet, you're not as inspired.
即便如此，你还是会有状态不佳的日子，比如你拖着沉重的脚步，灵感不那么迸发。

00:17:15.740 --> 00:17:24.500
One thing that would happen is, when people would come and visit, like if out of town, like some of my parents would drop by set or family friends or whatever who wanted to come by.
但有件事经常发生，那就是当有人来探班的时候，比如从外地来的人，我的父母或者亲友什么的顺道来看看。

00:17:24.500 --> 00:17:30.140
There was something about having the external, like when someone from Ohio comes to visit.
有些时候，当有了外部视角——比如当一个来自俄亥俄州的人来参观时。

00:17:30.140 --> 00:17:31.779
Yes, and you see it through their eyes.
没错，你会通过他们的眼睛来看待这一切。

00:17:31.779 --> 00:17:34.099
You see it through their eyes.
你通过他们的眼睛去审视。

00:17:34.099 --> 00:17:38.779
Those days were actually really interesting to me because I was like, oh, this is a cool job.
那些天对其实我来说真的很有趣，因为我会想：哦，这确实是一份很酷的工作。

00:17:38.779 --> 00:17:41.099
Like this is really interesting fun.
这真的是一项非常有趣好玩的工作。

00:17:41.099 --> 00:17:41.940
Yeah.
对。

00:17:41.940 --> 00:17:44.420
But you just, it's not that you take it for granted.
但这只是……并不是说你把它当成理所当然。

00:17:44.420 --> 00:17:48.140
It just, the repetition, it just becomes something.
只是日复一日的重复，它最终变成了一种……

00:17:48.140 --> 00:17:49.500
just becomes your life.
最终变成了你的生活。

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:51.339
It's your daily life, it's your normal.
这是你的日常生活，这是你的常态。

00:17:51.339 --> 00:17:55.740
And then every now and again, you're reminded, this is not normal in the best way possible.
然后偶尔，你会得到提醒：这可不是什么常态，这是最棒的那种不寻常。

00:17:55.740 --> 00:17:56.579
This is not normal.
这不是常态。

00:17:56.579 --> 00:17:59.180
This is really extraordinary what's happening here.
这里正在发生的事情真的是非同寻常。

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:00.380
And it's just human nature.
这只是人之常情。

00:18:00.380 --> 00:18:03.380
You do, you get used to stuff, you don't always appreciate the magic.
你确实会习惯一些事情，你并不总是能感激这份神奇。

00:18:03.380 --> 00:18:06.819
I'm coming, I'm like, parenthood is clicking into my brain here a little bit, right?
我就要说……这让我的脑海里联想到了一点育儿的经验，对吧？

00:18:06.819 --> 00:18:22.380
You have these amazing little humans and you sort of, in between those moments of like, wonder and appreciation, you're doing the grunt work of parenting and you're sometimes losing the magic of like what that is and then like something hits you and you're like, fuck, wait, this is the greatest thing in the world.
你拥有了这些可爱的小生命，在那些充满惊叹和感激的时刻之间，你正在做着养育孩子的繁重杂务，有时你甚至会忘记那种奇妙的感觉是什么，然后突然间有什么击中了你，你会想：“操，等等，这是世界上最棒的事情。”

00:18:22.380 --> 00:18:23.740
And it's akin to that.
这跟那种感觉很像。

00:18:23.740 --> 00:18:35.140
And it's almost like the grunt work is part of the magic because without that, it's like it doesn't, you know, if you just went.
而且可以说，这种繁重的杂务正是魔法的一部分，因为如果没有这个，它就像是……你知道的，如果你只是……

00:18:35.140 --> 00:18:36.539
You're earning the magic with the grunt work.
你用这些繁重的工作赢得了这份魔力。

00:18:36.539 --> 00:18:49.220
If you just went from triumph to triumph, let's say you were just like an actor that was just triumphant and you just won every award, Like, there would be something you would hate about that, eventually.
如果你只是从一个胜利走向另一个胜利，比如说你是一个一路高歌猛进、赢得所有奖项的演员，那么到最后，你一定会讨厌那种生活的。

00:18:49.220 --> 00:18:50.220
Yeah, oh yeah.
对，哦，是的。

00:18:50.220 --> 00:18:58.019
You'd be like, there's no, where's the struggle, where's the ascent, where's the resilience that I'm having to find, you know?
你会觉得：没有挑战，奋斗在哪里，攀登在哪里，我需要去寻找的韧性在哪里，你知道吗？

00:18:58.019 --> 00:18:59.019
Yeah.
对。

00:18:59.019 --> 00:19:05.220
It's a hard thing because it's hard to struggle, but without struggle, who are we?
这是一件艰难的事，因为挣扎很难，但如果没有挣扎，我们又是谁？

00:19:05.220 --> 00:19:06.779
We don't get forged, you know?
我们无法被塑造，你知道吗？

00:19:06.779 --> 00:19:08.299
Yeah, I think that's right.
对，我觉得确实如此。

00:19:08.299 --> 00:19:15.299
And I think we also made it hard on ourselves in a good way on how Mitch and Mother, because he didn't do the same episode every week.
而且我觉得我们在《老爸老妈浪漫史》中也以一种好的方式给自己制造了难度，因为我们每周拍的不是同一集。

00:19:15.299 --> 00:19:16.140
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

00:19:16.140 --> 00:19:16.980
It wasn't the cookie cutter.
它不是那种千篇一律的模式。

00:19:16.980 --> 00:19:19.619
Like here is basically what a himium episode is.
比如“老爸老妈浪漫史”的一集差不多就是这样。

00:19:19.619 --> 00:19:22.180
We're going to do this 200 times more or less.
我们要把这种模式再重复200次，差不多吧。

00:19:22.180 --> 00:19:23.019
We've really tried it.
我们真的尝试过了。

00:19:23.019 --> 00:19:27.819
We're always challenging yourself and almost like challenging every department.
我们总是在挑战自己，几乎是在挑战每一个部门。

00:19:27.819 --> 00:19:28.900
Absolutely.
绝对是的。

00:19:28.900 --> 00:19:32.819
The whole thing was challenged accepted and everyone accepted it and that's the magic.
整部剧的主旨就是“接受挑战”，每个人也都接受了，这就是魔法所在。

00:19:32.819 --> 00:19:41.779
We just talked about something borrowed, something blue, which is the one where Marshall shaved the landing strip in his head at the before the wedding, something borrowed.
我们刚才谈到了《借来的东西》（Something Borrowed），《蓝色诉求》（Something Blue），就是马修在婚礼前把头剃成飞机头的那一集……那是《借来的东西》。

00:19:41.779 --> 00:19:43.700
So it's some, it's the finale, right?
所以那是，那是季终集，对吧？

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:44.539
This season finale season.
这一季的季终集。

00:19:44.539 --> 00:19:45.619
I thought it was something borrowed, though.
不过我原以为那是《借来的东西》。

00:19:45.619 --> 00:19:47.619
Oh, something borrowed, right, yeah, isn't it?
哦，借来的东西，对吧，是的，是这样吗？

00:19:47.619 --> 00:19:49.019
Sorry, you're absolutely right.
抱歉，你完全说得对。

00:19:49.019 --> 00:19:50.420
Yeah, so something borrowed was...
对，所以借来的东西是……

00:19:50.420 --> 00:19:51.259
Second of all.
第二点。

00:19:51.259 --> 00:20:00.819
Jason gets the cool guy tips, he freaks out, and he takes the razor and he shaves that reverse mohawk in his head.
杰森得到了酷哥的建议，他吓坏了，然后他拿起剃须刀，在头上剃了个倒莫霍克发型。

00:20:00.819 --> 00:20:01.660
Yeah.
对。

00:20:01.660 --> 00:20:09.059
And I said to Craig, I was like, if you're in the hair department reading the script, you're like, oh shit.
我对克雷格说，我说，如果你在发型部门读剧本，你肯定会想，哦操。

00:20:09.059 --> 00:20:19.579
Like, we have to get frosted tips on Jason's hair somehow, and then we have to create an effect where he takes a razor.
就像，我们得想办法在杰森的头发上弄出挑染效果，然后我们还得创造一个他拿起剃须刀的效果。

00:20:21.099 --> 00:20:22.940
Jase is ahead.
杰斯先上了。

00:20:22.940 --> 00:20:23.779
Yeah.
对。

00:20:23.779 --> 00:20:27.460
Like, I mean, it was a huge ask of the makeup, I mean, that shot department.
我是说，这对化妆，我是说对那个拍摄部门来说是个巨大的要求。

00:20:27.460 --> 00:20:30.380
There should have been a special Emmy just for that shot, how well that went.
那个镜头应该专门得个艾美奖，拍得太好了。

00:20:30.380 --> 00:20:31.220
On the first try.
一次就过。

00:20:31.220 --> 00:20:33.819
We only did one take of it.
我们只拍了一条。

00:20:33.819 --> 00:20:36.259
And you can see me laughing for reals.
你可以看到我是真的在笑。

00:20:36.259 --> 00:20:37.619
Because it was a miracle.
因为那是个奇迹。

00:20:37.619 --> 00:20:39.500
We all be knew we had witnessed a miracle.
我们都知道我们见证了一个奇迹。

00:20:39.500 --> 00:20:40.339
Yeah.
对。

00:20:40.339 --> 00:20:42.059
What else?
还有呢？

00:20:42.059 --> 00:20:48.579
Paulo, I'd say, just as, hi Josh, hope you remember your concert in Sao Paulo, Brazil.
保罗，我想说，作为问候，嗨，乔什，希望你还记得你在巴西圣保罗的演唱会。

